    "cookingInstructions": "1. On order, trim the ends off and slice 2 appetizer buns into 12 equal slices to creating your crostini pieces.\nBrush one side of each slice with melted butter.\n2. Place the brie cheese wheel on a clean sanitized cutting board and carefully slice lines both vertically and\nhorizontally into the top layer of rind from the cheese making small squares and leaving you with the very\nsightly exposed inside of the cheese. Approximately 1-2 mm deep only just through the rind, not deep into the\ncheese wheel.\n3. Place the brie cheese into a black casserole dish with the exposed cheese facing upwards. Brush the exposed\ncheese with a light coating of the honey.\n4. Place the brie cheese in the oven until the brie cheese is warm, soft and slightly runny. (approx 8-9 minutes\ndepending on oven traffic). The finished brie should be very soft but still hold its shape.\n5. Place the crostini in the oven for 1-2 minutes until slightly crisped and golden but not crispy all the way\nthrough. The crostini should still be slightly soft in the centre but will crisp up as they cool.",
    "platingInstructions": "1. Place the casserole dish on a napkin lined medium spice plate.\n2. Fan the warm crostini’s in two rows of 6, around the casserole dish. Place a teaspoon next to the casserole\ndish\n3. Place the pepper jelly on top of the brie. The sauce should sit firm on top spread across the entire top of the\ncheese. Place the pesto in the centre.",
    "presentation": "The cheese is oven baked until hot and softened, then plated in a black casserole dish. The baked brie wheel is topped with cranberry sauce, and finished with orange zest. Served with 12 baked crostini's on a medium spice plate, secured with a beverage napkin and served with a teaspoon.",
