    "productKnowledge": "Sesame-soy seasoned Ahi served on fresh avocado, topped with sesame seeds. Served with fried wontons.",
    "cookTime": "2 - 3 minutes",
    "cookingInstructions": "1. On order, place the prepped tuna into a stainless steel mixing bowl. Ladle 1 fl. oz. of soy sesame\ndressing into the mixing bowl. Using a spoon, gently mix the tuna and the dressing together.\n2. Place the small diced avocado into a stainless steel mixing bowl. Ladle 0.5 fl. oz. of lime juice and\n1/4 tsp of fine sea salt into the mixing bowl. Using a spoon, gently mix the avocado together with lime\njuice and salt.\n3. Place the forming tool onto the chilled plate. Place the diced avocado inside the tool and onto the plate.\nEnsure you press down on the avocado slightly. You want the avocado to be level inside the forming tool once it\nis all in place.\n4. Now place the dressed tuna on top of the dressed avocado. As with the avocado, ensure the tuna is spread\nout evenly in the forming tool and the top is level.",
    "platingInstructions": "1. Place the prepped wonton crisps to one side of the forming tool.\n2. Carefully remove the forming tool by pulling it up from the base of the plate.\n3. Sprinkle the top of the tuna with white sesame seeds.\n4. Place one lime wedge onto the plate beside the tartare.",
    "presentation": "Served on a medium spice plate. Seasoned and lightly tossed in a soy sesame dressing, the Ahi Tuna is placed over-top of a creamy avocado bed. Served with fried wontons and garnished with sesame seeds and a lime wedge.",
