    "cookingInstructions": "1. On order, butter brush the bottom of a pie plate or oven pan. Next, brush the top of the salmon with the\nhoney mustard glaze.\n2. Place the coated salmon filet into the pie plate or oven pan. Place the pie plate or oven pan into the oven\nand allow the salmon to cook.\n3. Once the salmon is just cooked, remove it from the oven and set it aside. The salmon should take\napproximately 10 - 12 minutes depending on oven traffic. Once removed, brush with additional glaze if\nneeded.\n4. With 2 minutes remaining in the cook time of the salmon, place the broccoli in the steamer and cook until\ntender yet crisp. Season with olive oil / canola blend, salt and pepper.",
    "platingInstructions": "1. Neatly place the garlic mashed potatoes to the middle-part of the plate.\n2. Neatly place the oiled and seasoned broccoli beside the garlic mashed potatoes in the middle-part of the\nplate.\n3. Carefully remove the cooked salmon from the pie plate or oven pan using a metal spatula, and place it on\ntop of the garlic mashed potatoes and broccoli. Note: the skin is to remain in the pie plate or oven pan. The\nsalmon is always to be served with the skin removed.\n4. Finish the presentation by placing a lemon wedge beside the mashed potatoes.",
