    "productKnowledge": "DESSERTS A shareable platter consisting of our house-made Crème Brule, torched with sugar for a crisp crust, a cheesecake topped with raspberry coulis, our legendary Keg Billy Miner Pie, topped with fudge, caramel, and toast almonds.",
    "cookTime": "4 - 5 minutes",
    "cookingInstructions": "1. On order, remove a Crème Brulée from the refrigerator and place on the plate. Cover the surface of the\nCrème Brulée with white sugar. Ensure that the entire surface of the Crème Brulée has been covered with\nsugar. Using a Crème Brulée torch, heat the sugar until melted and golden brown.\n2. Obtain 1 cheesecake from the walk-in cooler, and carefully remove the plastic wrap and cardboard ring.\nRemove the silicone paper strip.\n3. Follow the pre-scored markings on your Billy Miner Pie and cut accordingly.\n4. Portions may be pre-cut and plated, or may be cut to order. Either way, be sure that accurate size portions\nare marked to reduce waste.",
    "platingInstructions": "1. Place the Billy Miner Pie in the centre of the plate with the point towards 6o'clock. Zigzag hot fudge and\ncaramel sauce in opposite directions over top of the pie and the plate. Sprinkle toasted almonds over the pie.\n2. Place the portion of cheesecake on the plate standing up on the left side of the billy miner. With the point\nfacing 11o'clock\n3. Ladle the coulis over the middle of the cheesecake so that the topping runs down the sides of the cake and\npools on both sides.\n4. Place a folded cocktail napkin on the right side of the billy miner and place the finished brulee on top.\n5. Finish with the mint sprig and orange wheel.",
    "presentation": "All three deserts are plated attractively on a chilled black rimmed plate. and The crème Brulé is torched and served with a mint sprig and orange ed wheel, the cheesecake is topped with raspberry coulis, and the Billy Miner Pie is dressed with hot fudge, caramel, and toasted almonds. The dessert platter is served on the wooden spinner.",
